                                  MENUITEM=
 
Adds a choice to the startup menu.  Used only in a menu block.

\bSyntax\p

    MENUITEM=blockname[,menutext]

\bParameters\p

blockname
    The block of CONFIG.SYS lines the choice uses.  A block that is not
    in the file is reported and left off the menu.

menutext
    What the menu shows for the choice.  Defaults to the block name if
    none specified.

A menu has up to nine choices.

\bRelated Commands\p

<\aSUBMENU=\vSUBMENU=\v> adds a choice that opens another menu.  See
<\aMultiple Configurations\vMulti-config\v>.
 
                                     
