                                  NULLTRAP=
 
Stops a 32-bit program that writes through a null pointer.

\bSyntax\p

    NULLTRAP=ON | OFF

\bParameters\p

ON
    Prevents 32-bit programs from writing to the first bytes of memory,
    which can destroy the first interrupt vectors.  
    This is the default setting.

OFF
    For a program that writes to low memory on purpose.
 
